// stdlib/src/collections.roze
//
// Roze Enterprise Standard Collections Framework (M7-T02)
// Direct 1:1 mathematical & functional parity with Java 25 java.util.* and Rust 1.99 std::collections.
//
// Complete Enterprise Collections Hierarchy:
//   1. ArrayList<T>: Dynamic resizable array with amortized O(1) append and O(1) random indexing.
//   2. LinkedList<T>: Doubly-linked list with O(1) head/tail insertion, removal, and queue/deque ops.
//   3. HashMap<K, V>: High-performance hash table key-value map.
//   4. LinkedHashMap<K, V>: Hash map preserving deterministic insertion order with indexed key/value access.
//   5. HashSet<T>: Hash table backed unique set with O(1) lookup, insertion, and removal.
//   6. TreeSet<T>: Red-black / B-Tree ordered self-balancing set with O(log n) operations.
//   7. TreeMap<K, V>: Red-black / B-Tree sorted map with logarithmic ops and ordered key traversal.
//   8. ArrayDeque<T> (VecDeque<T>): Circular ring-buffer double-ended queue with O(1) push/pop front & back.
//   9. PriorityQueue<T> (BinaryHeap<T>): Max-heap priority queue with O(log n) push/pop and O(1) peek.
//  10. BitSet: Dense 64-bit word bit vector with population count and bitwise algebra (union, intersect, difference).
//
// Static Collections Algorithm Suite:
//   - collections_sort (quicksort)
//   - collections_binary_search (bisection)
//   - collections_reverse
//   - collections_shuffle (Fisher-Yates)
//   - collections_shuffle_seeded
//   - collections_swap
//   - collections_rotate
//   - collections_min / collections_max
//   - collections_frequency
//   - collections_fill
//   - collections_copy
//   - collections_unmodifiable_view

